This repository is the original VIGIL template, not an observing node.

The presence of this file makes `_gate.yml` deny schedule-triggered captures.
Manual dispatch still works, so the ability to capture from here is not lost;
what is lost is automatic capture, which a template has no business doing.

It is checked by file rather than by repository name on purpose: a name stops
matching the moment someone renames or transfers the repository, and the
template would then start scraping without anyone having decided that. A file
survives both, and shows up in the diff when removed.

`bootstrap.yml` deletes this file in every repository created from the
template. That is the exact moment a copy stops being a template and becomes
a node.
